A||||23||fldevel||Quest to make a 10 second fiero ||||1||
Z||000000||fldevel||07-11-2001||02:43 PM|||| is this posible to make a 10 sec fiero with the stock 2.8 block .. also .. what would your suggestions be for turbos,NOS systes etc.. the quest has begun.. <P> do i put too many "...... " in my sentences ??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Neal||07-11-2001||03:57 PM||||someone just watched fast and the furious...<P>but seriously without BIG CASH i dont think it can be done. i think around 650-750hp would put a fiero into the 10's.<P>start with a 3.4, turbo @ 15psi AND 2 stage n2o, 150 shot followed by a 100 shot.  100% forged bottom end, ARP rod bolts, main studs, and head studs, a top quality port job, a totally custom intake and exaust.<P>That MAY give you an engine that can crack into the 10's.  But then there is the tranny, for a solid run you would need a limited slip rear end.  You can getem put on the fiero tranny, but it will still be so weak that i dont think it could hold up for more than a couple runs||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||07-11-2001||04:35 PM||||i'm not sure that the engine will last... but a true 6 fogger nitrous system would surley put it there... but the rod bearings are known to fail and under load you'd be hard pressed to hold them where their at with a shock like that...<P>once my car is back on the ground i'll let ya know what i'm running...  i'm at 279hp-312lbft on nitrous... shootin for high 12s... but not sure how thats gunna work out.. my 17's didn't hook up for crap.. i hope the bigger stickyer ones will. if not.. i need a set of stock 4cy stamped 14" steel wheels... any one in the ATL. have a pair they'll donate to the 12 second cause. BF_G drag radials will be perfect on those... ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fldevel||07-11-2001||04:57 PM||||money isint a problem here...and we are planning  on a completly custom motor job but the block HAS to be a stock 2.8 if at all posible .. i own the car but it will be a group project so i think i should have enough founds to get it done .. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||07-11-2001||05:16 PM||||if you are serious about this you need to be thinking HP to weight ratio - not simply max HP.<P> the Fiero weights between 2500 and 2900 lbs depending on year and model<P>  its a very heavy little car<P> strip the body panels out and drill out the space frame till it looks the the frame of the hindenberg<P>   and know that you are making it spindly while you are doing this<P>  but then again, drag racers (rails) are not designed to survive a 40mph crash into a brick wall either<P>  in fact you should probally replace the whole frame.<P>  also all the windows, the seats gotta go, interior, radio, battery, headlights and taillights<P>  I read once you can get fiberglass body replacement sections that are lighter than the stock plastic ones too.<P>when you get all done it might still look like a fiero from a standoff distance - but there wont be many fiero parts left in it.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||87FieroGTx||07-11-2001||07:13 PM|||| Start with the 2.8 bore and stroke it to 3.2/3.3 forged bottom end ported intake / TB / heads get the 550hp turbo everyone is talking about 3.5" exaust and go with a built AUTO they will hold the HP your looking for with these mods you will be there or close to it.<P> It will probably cost you 10k.<P> You should have 600 - 650hp with that setup. <P> Weight reduction 101<P> Take out the trunk, spare tire, jack, get light weight seats (1 seat) and wheels remove the carpets and stickers contrary to popular belief they actually ADD weight and wind resistance and make you slower <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||07-11-2001||07:53 PM||||How many times does it have to run 10's?<P>JATO will work once.....||||reg||1
Z||000007||Spektyr||07-11-2001||09:03 PM||||Actually, you can get N size model rocket motors a lot cheaper (and legally) than JATO's.  48" long with 1000lbs of thrust.  4-6 of those mounted solidly to the frame with the ignitors wired into a WOT switch.<P>Mash the pedal to the floor, all rocket motors light, and POOF!  You're flying down the track.  Just make sure they're angled slightly down so you're not flying ABOVE the track.<P>Oh, and needless to say, don't install the explosive charge at the end used to blow the nose cone off the rocket...<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Shaun41178||07-11-2001||10:59 PM||||Well I have a Direct replacement GM block that can probably handle upwards of 500 hp.  Its the aluminum one and is brand new.<P>If money is no object and you have the funds you should go with the aluminum block, aluminum heads for the flow, forged pistons rods and a Scat forged crank.  Extrude hone everything and run a direct port nitrous kit set at aorund 200 hp or more even or a big @ss turbo with insane boost.  Use an auto tranny from JPT and lighten the car up.<P>If you want my block it will cost you $2500 shipped to your front door.  New they were over $4k.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||00lE||07-12-2001||07:15 AM||||I have heard rumors that GM no longer makes some of the parts need to build that block.  Main bearings or something like that.  May want to check that out before making such a sizable investment.||||reg||1
Z||000010||88 Fiero||07-12-2001||06:52 PM||||If you want a 500 horses on a fiero check this website. A guy I think from netherlands makes a turbo for the fiero that can crank out 500 horses... <A HREF="http://wwnet.fi/amworks" TARGET=_blank>http://wwnet.fi/amworks</A>  <BR>the kit is price around $4,800.00. You still need to do some modifications to the engine to be able to handle it.<P>Good Luck!!<p>[This message has been edited by 88 Fiero (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||fldevel||07-12-2001||06:53 PM||||lol ok ok .. here is there deal .. our goal is to make a everyday driver yet have the car still run at least low 12s r so to be more realistic .. also we are talking about the alum block Shaun41178 we are un-decided about that at this point .. the doner car is my old 86 2m4 witch looks like itl be a decent little doner so far also thinking of making a custom removible top on the car .. i think it will look sweet when it is finished .. sorry for the long post .. im getting excited already :P<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Mach10||07-12-2001||06:57 PM||||Bowtie alum. block with 4-bolt mains, for sure. <P>Drop compression to 8:1, and slap on 63lbs of boost. Worked for F-1, and they were only 1.6 liter 6's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
